Short sword would be a waste. Long sword has things like Frost Brand and
Fire Brand in it that you might want. Your first sacrifice gift will
be Cleaver, though, which uses axe skill; it's actually not the worst
choice, though you might decide against it because it is two-handed.
I've used Cleaver until Stormbringer when playing barbarians. 

> My current AC is 0 and I have some useful wands. Will I be able to
> handle the top level of Soko? assuming I can fix my mistake.

Depends on XL and what gets generated. If you take advantage of the door
chokepoint you should be OK, but don't be afraid to run. 

> Also I havent found any shops yet, it there any other way to ID scrolls
> other than reading them? I have a bunch I would like to figuyre out.

You can ID scare monster by dropping it. You can ID others by seeing
monsters read them (create monster, teleportation, earth). You can make
guesses based on the number of scrolls you have --- 3 scrolls named ANDOVA
BEGARIN are much more likely to be identify than genocide.  But really,
go to Minetown. You should also be able to pick up better armor off of
dwarves on your way down.

I would finish Sokoban since I was already there, but that's up to you,
and others might have differing opinions.

